MiniCPM-o 4.5 on vLLM-Omni: text-only duplex sessions end at Stage 0 (the Thinker), and a Thinker-only pipeline.

Apply to the vLLM-Omni install of the agent server (or to an overlay copy of it), from its site-packages directory:

    cd <env>/lib/python3.12/site-packages && patch -p1 < .../patches/minicpmo_thinker_only.patch

Needs the duplex patches (input clock, token trace, MiniCPM-o support: upstream PR vllm-project/vllm-omni#8485 and
its follow-ups, or fork williamLyh/vllm-omni branch duplex-input-clock). Independent of
minicpmo_fe_per_session.patch (different files); apply both. Same change as the authors' RL server overlay
edits 5-6 (text_only_sessions()) and the fork patch fp/0006; not upstream.

- Generic engine part (opt-in per plugin): DuplexModelPlugin.text_output_stage_id. A session whose output modalities
  exclude audio gets final_stage_id = that stage for its stage requests: the orchestrator never forwards to (or
  prewarms) the later stages, and the input clock acknowledges a unit at its Stage-0 segment end.
- MiniCPM-o part: text_output_stage_id = 0; the data plane turns each finished Stage-0 segment into the unit's
  transcript (the same slice llm2tts hands the Talker), sent as response.output_audio_transcript.delta without audio;
  a unit <|speak|><|turn_eos|><|listen|> is a speaking unit that ends the turn.
- pipeline "minicpmo_4_5_thinker" (deploy yaml `pipeline:`, with `async_chunk: false`): the stock pipeline cut to
  Stage 0, so a text-only server needs one GPU and no Talker / Code2Wav (configs/minicpmo_4_5_thinker_1gpu.yaml).
Audio sessions are unchanged: on the two-GPU deployment, text-only sessions also stop at Stage 0.

Measured (2x RTX 5090, 2026-10-04): on one deployment, text-only sessions with and
without this patch give bit-identical Thinker tokens, decisions, text and logprobs. The Thinker-only deployment is
NOT bit-identical to the two-GPU one: inputs are identical, but from the first speak unit the logprobs differ at
bf16 level (mean |diff| 0.013 over the first 24 tokens, max 0.14; single stage without async_chunk takes another
scheduling / kernel path), so sampled trajectories diverge; behaviour statistics match.

